The shop assistant comes back from the stockroom.
She has the yellow shirt in size L.
She gives me the shirt.
"Here is the right size," she says.
I thank her.
This time, I go into the fitting room.
I take off my jacket.
Then I try on the new shirt.
I look in the mirror.
I am relieved.
It fits perfectly!
The shoulders are not too tight now.
This shirt is much better than the first one.
I take the shirt off again.
I leave the cubicle.
I go back to customer service, not to the till.
The shop assistant is waiting there for me.
